Fast terminal with tabs, split panes and sessions that survive disconnects

WezTerm is a terminal emulator that draws text with the GPU and has a multiplexer built in, so tabs, panes and windows can run on a local or remote server and be reattached later. It is configured with a single file that reloads as you edit it.

- Tabs, split panes and multiple windows
- Multiplexing on local and remote hosts over SSH or TLS
- Font ligatures, color emoji and true color
- Searchable scrollback and clickable hyperlinks
- Built-in SSH client and serial port connections
- Inline images with the iTerm2, Kitty and Sixel protocols
